{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00631",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.53,
      "end_seconds": 10.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "Hi doctor. Sorry, I know it's silly, but I can't stop sneezing and I'm starting to panic a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.14,
      "end_seconds": 18.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Not silly at all. Tell me about the sneezing. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.88,
      "end_seconds": 33.83,
      "duration_seconds": 14.95,
      "text": "It comes in fits. Like, I'll sneeze eight or nine times in a row, and then my eyes stream and my nose runs like a tap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.22,
      "end_seconds": 40.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.25,
      "end_seconds": 49.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "Since the start of September. So about three weeks, I think. Maybe more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.51,
      "end_seconds": 58.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Does it come at any particular time of day, or in particular places?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.34,
      "end_seconds": 69.93,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "Mornings, mostly, and when I'm outside walking the dog. It's much better when I'm indoors with the windows shut."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.72,
      "end_seconds": 75.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "That's helpful, that's a clear pattern. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.0,
      "end_seconds": 87.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "My mate reckons it's hay fever, but I've never had it before, I'm twenty-nine, so I don't know. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.85,
      "end_seconds": 99.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.39,
      "text": "People can develop it later, it's not unusual. Let me have a look up your nose. Tilt your head back. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.57,
      "end_seconds": 104.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Okay. Is this going to hurt? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.1,
      "end_seconds": 123.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Not at all, it's just a light. Keep still."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.96,
      "end_seconds": 129.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Is everything all right in there? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.47,
      "end_seconds": 149.85,
      "duration_seconds": 10.38,
      "text": "The lining of your nose is pale and a bit swollen on both sides. Nothing blocking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.69,
      "end_seconds": 153.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Is that bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.16,
      "end_seconds": 163.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "No, it's what I'd expect with a lot of sneezing, and there's nothing sinister. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.58,
      "end_seconds": 174.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.61,
      "text": "I just wanted to make sure it wasn't something serious, like a growth or something. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.25,
      "end_seconds": 183.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "Nothing here suggests that at all. Try not to google it at midnight. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.68,
      "end_seconds": 188.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Too late, I did. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.56,
      "end_seconds": 197.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Everyone does. What sort of dog have you got, by the way? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.01,
      "end_seconds": 209.52,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "A spaniel called Biscuit. She's a nightmare in the long grass, she comes back covered in seeds. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.12,
      "end_seconds": 220.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "Spaniels are brilliant at collecting whatever's floating about outside, so that fits with your pattern. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.47,
      "end_seconds": 225.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "She does love a hedge. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.56,
      "end_seconds": 238.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "Right. Well, to find out what is triggering it, I'd like to arrange a skin prick test."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.56,
      "end_seconds": 242.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "What happens in that? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.24,
      "end_seconds": 262.75,
      "duration_seconds": 18.51,
      "text": "We put tiny drops of common triggers like pollen and dust on your forearm and prick the skin lightly. A few spots go red and itchy, and that tells us what you react to. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.92,
      "end_seconds": 268.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "That doesn't sound too bad. When? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.6,
      "end_seconds": 282.27,
      "duration_seconds": 12.67,
      "text": "The nurse will book you in, within a fortnight or so. Don't take any antihistamines for three days beforehand, or the test won't work."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.23,
      "end_seconds": 287.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Okay. And meanwhile? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.39,
      "end_seconds": 299.39,
      "duration_seconds": 11.0,
      "text": "Keep the windows shut in the morning, shower and change when you get in from the dog walk, and wash the dog's bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.69,
      "end_seconds": 306.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "That I can do. Will it go away? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.02,
      "end_seconds": 321.53,
      "duration_seconds": 12.51,
      "text": "Most people get it under control once we know the trigger. I'd like to see you again in three weeks to go over the test."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.93,
      "end_seconds": 328.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Three weeks. Great. Thanks, doctor, I feel calmer now. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.49,
      "end_seconds": 334.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Good. Go and enjoy the dog. ~"
    }
  ]
}
